# POST /owners (Create Owner) — Exploration Report

## 1. YAML defining POST /owners

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`**

This is an OfficeFloor "WoOF" flow. It authorizes on role `OWNER_ADMIN`, then chains named steps (each `next:` points to the following step), all governed by a `transaction`:

```yaml
composition:
  authorize: "hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')"

validate:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.ValidateOwnerFields
  next: ensureUniqueTelephone

ensureUniqueTelephone:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.EnsureTelephoneUnique
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: ensureUniqueHousehold

ensureUniqueHousehold:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.EnsureHouseholdUnique
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: ensureCityCapacity

ensureCityCapacity:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.EnsureCityCapacity
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: build

build:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.BuildOwner
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: assignCode

assignCode:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.AssignCustomerCode
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: assignHousehold

assignHousehold:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.AssignHouseholdId
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: countNamesakes

countNamesakes:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.CountNamesakes
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: save

save:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.SaveOwner
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: respond

respond:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.RespondWithOwnerCreated
  govern: [ transaction ]
```

The `{ownerId}.PUT.yml` (update) and `owners.GET.yml` (list) files exist alongside it in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/`.

## 2. Java function classes referenced by the POST /owners YAML

All under `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/`. The OfficeFloor pattern: each class has a single `service(...)` method; `@RequestBody` binds the HTTP body, `@Val`/`Out<T>` are OfficeFloor pipeline variables (a step's `Out<T>` becomes a downstream `@Val T`), and repository/mapper parameters are dependency-injected Spring beans.

**ValidateOwnerFields.java** — normalizes address, validates required fields, normalizes telephone to E.164 and email; publishes the validated `OwnerFieldsDto`.
```java
public class ValidateOwnerFields {
    public void service(@RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto request, Out<OwnerFieldsDto> validated)
            throws MissingOwnerFieldsException, InvalidTelephoneException, InvalidEmailException {
        request.setAddress(OwnerAddress.normalize(request.getAddress()));
        List<String> missing = new ArrayList<>();
        require("firstName", request.getFirstName(), missing);
        require("lastName", request.getLastName(), missing);
        require("address", request.getAddress(), missing);
        require("city", request.getCity(), missing);
        require("telephone", request.getTelephone(), missing);
        if (!missing.isEmpty()) {
            throw new MissingOwnerFieldsException(missing);
        }
        request.setTelephone(OwnerTelephone.toE164(request.getTelephone()));
        request.setEmail(OwnerEmail.normalize(request.getEmail()));
        validated.set(request);
    }
    private static void require(String field, String value, List<String> missing) {
        if (value == null || value.isBlank()) { missing.add(field); }
    }
}
```

**EnsureTelephoneUnique.java** — rejects duplicate E.164 telephone (throws `DuplicateTelephoneException`, 409).
```java
public class EnsureTelephoneUnique {
    public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerRepository ownerRepository)
            throws DuplicateTelephoneException {
        String telephone = canonical(request.getTelephone());
        for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
            if (telephone.equals(canonical(existing.getTelephone()))) {
                throw new DuplicateTelephoneException(request.getTelephone());
            }
        }
    }
    private static String canonical(String value) {
        try { return OwnerTelephone.toE164(value); }
        catch (InvalidTelephoneException ex) {
            return value == null ? "" : value.replaceAll("\\D", "");
        }
    }
}
```

**EnsureHouseholdUnique.java** — rejects same lastName+address unless `sharesHousehold:true` (throws `DuplicateHouseholdException`, 409).
```java
public class EnsureHouseholdUnique {
    public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerRepository ownerRepository)
            throws DuplicateHouseholdException {
        if (Boolean.TRUE.equals(request.getSharesHousehold())) { return; }
        String lastName = normalize(request.getLastName());
        String address = OwnerAddress.normalize(request.getAddress());
        for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
            if (lastName.equals(normalize(existing.getLastName()))
                    && address.equals(OwnerAddress.normalize(existing.getAddress()))) {
                throw new DuplicateHouseholdException(request.getLastName(), request.getAddress());
            }
        }
    }
    private static String normalize(String value) {
        if (value == null) { return ""; }
        return value.trim().replaceAll("\\s+", " ").toLowerCase();
    }
}
```

**EnsureCityCapacity.java** — rejects when the city already holds `CityAtCapacityException.CAPACITY` (50) owners (throws `CityAtCapacityException`, 409).
```java
public class EnsureCityCapacity {
    public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerRepository ownerRepository)
            throws CityAtCapacityException {
        String city = normalize(request.getCity());
        int count = 0;
        for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
            if (city.equals(normalize(existing.getCity()))) { count++; }
        }
        if (count >= CityAtCapacityException.CAPACITY) {
            throw new CityAtCapacityException(request.getCity(), count);
        }
    }
    private static String normalize(String value) {
        return value == null ? "" : value.trim().toLowerCase();
    }
}
```

**BuildOwner.java** — maps DTO to entity and defaults `registrationDate` to today. This is the key place the created-date is set.
```java
public class BuildOwner {
    public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerMapper ownerMapper, Out<Owner> built) {
        Owner owner = ownerMapper.toOwner(request);
        if (owner.getRegistrationDate() == null) {
            owner.setRegistrationDate(LocalDate.now());
        }
        built.set(owner);
    }
}
```

**AssignCustomerCode.java** — sets `customerCode` as `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`.
```java
public class AssignCustomerCode {
    public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
        String city = owner.getCity();
        String city3 = city.substring(0, Math.min(3, city.length())).toUpperCase();
        String lastName = owner.getLastName();
        String last3 = lastName.substring(0, Math.min(3, lastName.length())).toUpperCase();
        long sequence = ownerRepository.findAll().stream()
                .filter(existing -> city.equalsIgnoreCase(existing.getCity()))
                .count() + 1;
        owner.setCustomerCode(String.format("%s-%s-%04d", city3, last3, sequence));
    }
}
```

**AssignHouseholdId.java** — assigns a shared `householdId` (SHA-256-derived) to household peers, back-filling existing members.
```java
public class AssignHouseholdId {
    public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
        String lastName = normalize(owner.getLastName());
        String address = OwnerAddress.normalize(owner.getAddress());
        List<Owner> household = new ArrayList<>();
        for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
            if (lastName.equals(normalize(existing.getLastName()))
                    && address.equals(OwnerAddress.normalize(existing.getAddress()))) {
                household.add(existing);
            }
        }
        if (household.isEmpty()) { return; }
        String householdId = deriveHouseholdId(lastName, address);
        owner.setHouseholdId(householdId);
        for (Owner existing : household) {
            if (existing.getHouseholdId() == null || existing.getHouseholdId().isBlank()) {
                existing.setHouseholdId(householdId);
                ownerRepository.save(existing);
            }
        }
    }
    private static String deriveHouseholdId(String lastName, String address) {
        try {
            byte[] digest = MessageDigest.getInstance("SHA-256")
                    .digest((lastName + '|' + address).getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8));
            StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder("H-");
            for (int i = 0; i < 6; i++) { sb.append(String.format("%02X", digest[i])); }
            return sb.toString();
        } catch (NoSuchAlgorithmException ex) {
            throw new IllegalStateException("SHA-256 not available", ex);
        }
    }
    private static String normalize(String value) {
        if (value == null) { return ""; }
        return value.trim().replaceAll("\\s+", " ").toLowerCase();
    }
}
```

**CountNamesakes.java** — sets `namesakeCount` (existing owners with same first+last name; runs before save so new owner not counted).
```java
public class CountNamesakes {
    public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
        int count = 0;
        for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
            if (equalsIgnoreCase(owner.getFirstName(), existing.getFirstName())
                    && equalsIgnoreCase(owner.getLastName(), existing.getLastName())) {
                count++;
            }
        }
        owner.setNamesakeCount(count);
    }
    private static boolean equalsIgnoreCase(String a, String b) {
        return a == null ? b == null : a.equalsIgnoreCase(b);
    }
}
```

**SaveOwner.java** — persists the owner.
```java
public class SaveOwner {
    public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
        ownerRepository.save(owner);
    }
}
```

**RespondWithOwnerCreated.java** — maps to `OwnerDto` and returns HTTP 201 Created with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.
```java
public class RespondWithOwnerCreated {
    public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerMapper ownerMapper,
            ObjectResponse<ResponseEntity<OwnerDto>> response) {
        OwnerDto dto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
        response.send(ResponseEntity.created(URI.create("/api/owners/" + owner.getId())).body(dto));
    }
}
```

**Package-private helpers** used by the above (same directory):
- **OwnerAddress.java** — `normalize(...)`: trims/collapses whitespace, upper-cases, expands `ST→STREET, RD→ROAD, AVE→AVENUE`.
- **OwnerTelephone.java** — `toE164(...)`: strips formatting, assumes `+61` for national numbers dropping a leading `0`; validates `\+[0-9]{8,15}`; throws `InvalidTelephoneException`.
- **OwnerEmail.java** — `normalize(...)`: null/blank → null; otherwise validates syntax and lower-cases; throws `InvalidEmailException`.

## 3. Owner entity — registration/created date

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`** (extends `Person`, which supplies `firstName`/`lastName`; `BaseEntity` supplies `id`/`isNew()`).

The created-date field is `registrationDate` (there is no separate "created" field):
```java
@Column(name = "registration_date")
private LocalDate registrationDate;

public LocalDate getRegistrationDate() { return this.registrationDate; }
public void setRegistrationDate(LocalDate registrationDate) { this.registrationDate = registrationDate; }
```
Other create-relevant columns with getters/setters: `address`, `city`, `telephone` (`@Pattern "^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$"`), `email`, `customerCode`, `householdId`, `namesakeCount` (Integer), and `pets`. `registrationDate` is set in `BuildOwner` (defaults to `LocalDate.now()`), and consumed by `OwnerMapper.membershipNumber(...)`.

## 4. OwnerRepository interface

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java`** — plain interface (not `@Repository`-annotated here), all methods `throws DataAccessException`:
- `Collection<Owner> findByLastName(String lastName)`
- `Page<Owner> findByLastName(String lastName, Pageable pageable)`
- `Owner findById(int id)`
- `void save(Owner owner)`
- `Collection<Owner> findAll()`
- `Page<Owner> findAll(Pageable pageable)`
- `void delete(Owner owner)`

The POST flow uses `findAll()` (uniqueness/count/capacity checks) and `save(Owner)`. Implementations exist at `repository/jpa/JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`, `repository/jdbc/JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`, and `repository/springdatajpa/SpringDataOwnerRepository.java`.

## 5. Escalation YAMLs and handlers

Directory: **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/`**. Each YAML is named for the fully-qualified exception class it maps, and simply points to a handler class. All 11:
- `java.lang.Exception.yml`
- `org.springframework.dao.DataIntegrityViolationException.yml`
- `...rest.escalation.CityAtCapacityException.yml`
- `...rest.escalation.DuplicateHouseholdException.yml`
- `...rest.escalation.DuplicateTelephoneException.yml`
- `...rest.escalation.InvalidEmailException.yml`
- `...rest.escalation.InvalidTelephoneException.yml`
- `...rest.escalation.MissingOwnerFieldsException.yml`
- `...rest.escalation.NotFoundException.yml`
- `org.springframework.security.authorization.AuthorizationDeniedException.yml`
- `org.springframework.web.bind.MethodArgumentNotValidException.yml`

Full example — `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.MissingOwnerFieldsException.yml`:
```yaml
handle:
